Package: stanliWebR
Title: Sample brms and rbmi Models with stanli in WebAssembly
Version: 0.10.1
Authors@R: c(person("Lukas", "Widmer", email = "lukas_andreas.widmer@novartis.com",
                    role = c("aut", "cre")),
             person("Novartis", "Pharma AG", role = "cph"))
Author: Lukas Widmer [aut, cre],
  Novartis Pharma AG [cph]
Maintainer: Lukas Widmer <lukas_andreas.widmer@novartis.com>
Description: rbmi hands a Stan program to rstan, which compiles it with a C++
    toolchain and so cannot work in WebAssembly. This package swaps the few package
    internals that compile and sample for equivalents that run the same program
    through stanli, a Stan interpreter, and hand back an ordinary rstan 'stanfit'.
    Everything downstream -- rbmi's diagnostics and draw extraction, and so on -- is
    the package's own code. RBesT and OncoBayes2, which sample precompiled models
    with rstan::sampling(), are routed to stanli the same way, and so are rstan's own
    stan_model() and sampling(). brms has a stanli backend of its own: this package
    makes it the default and samples its chains on webR workers.
    Loading the package arranges for each of them to be
    patched whenever it is loaded, so brm(), rbmi::method_bayes(), RBesT::gMAP(),
    OncoBayes2::blrm_exnex() and rstan::stan_model() work unchanged. These packages,
    rstan and stanli are listed under Suggests only so
    that the package installs outside WebAssembly; the patches report what they
    could not find.
